id: pm-8nev0o
title: "A budget-truncated read is resumable on one surface and terminal on five, and the only recovery the envelope names is to abandon the budget that truncated it"
description: "Every bounded read declares two truncation mechanisms and only one of them is resumable, but the envelope reports both through the same flag pair, so a caller cannot tell a page it can continue from a page it cannot.\n\n## What is measured\n\nAt HEAD build 2026.8.14, on this 2,482-item workspace.\n\nWhen the row limit is what truncates, the envelope carries a usable continuation cursor:\n\n    pm list --status open --limit 10 --json\n      -> count 10, has_more true, truncated true,\n         next_cursor \"eyJ2ZXJzaW9uIjoxLCJmaW5nZXJwcmludCI6ImVjMzAy...\"\n\nWhen the token budget is what truncates, the same three flags are set and the cursor is null:\n\n    pm list --status open --limit 500 --json\n      -> count 85 of total 343, has_more true, truncated true,\n         next_cursor null,\n         output_budget_truncation.reason \"output_budget_reached\"\n         output_budget_truncation.restore_with\n           \"Re-run with --output-budget unbounded for the complete result.\"\n\nThe two cases are distinguishable only by reaching into output_budget_truncation, a key that is absent on the resumable case. Nothing in the flag pair the pagination contract is written against separates them.\n\n## The population this makes unreadable\n\nThe surface that serves the historical record is the worst case measured:\n\n    pm list-closed --limit 3000 --json\n      -> 4 rows of total 2125, has_more true, next_cursor null\n\nFour rows of 2,125 is 0.19 percent of the population, and the only recovery the envelope names is to abandon the budget:\n\n    default budget      28,073 bytes    ~7,018 tokens     4 rows\n    --output-budget unbounded  15,918,262 bytes  ~3,979,565 tokens  2125 rows\n    amplification       567x\n\nThere is no intermediate. A caller that needs row 5 must either accept a 3.98 million token response or give up. At the declared million-item scale target the ratio is not a constant, and the prescribed recovery is the exact behaviour the budget exists to prevent.\n\n## Why this is not the sibling that already shipped\n\npm-jt8aa2 closed on 2026-08-13 having shipped the disclosure block quoted above. Its third acceptance criterion reads: \"has_more true is never emitted without either a usable continuation cursor or a named alternative recovery path\". The disjunction is satisfied by restore_with, so the item is correctly closed on its own terms. This item owns the half the disjunction permitted: the named alternative is the only alternative, and it is unbounded.\n\n## The inconsistency that proves it is not a design constraint\n\nOne command already does it correctly. Under the identical reason code, pm context emits both:\n\n    pm context --limit 50 --json\n      -> has_more true,\n         output_budget_truncation.reason \"output_budget_reached\",\n         next_cursor \"eyJ2ZXJzaW9uIjoxLCJmaW5nZXJwcmludCI6IjllZDJm...\"\n\nMeasured across the read surfaces:\n\n    surface        budget-truncated   cursor emitted\n    list                 yes               no\n    list-open            yes               no\n    list-all             yes               no\n    list-closed          yes               no\n    next                 yes               no\n    context              yes              YES\n    search               no (limit)       YES\n\nSo a budget-truncated read can carry a continuation cursor. Five surfaces do not, and the one that does proves the capability exists in the same code path.\n\n## Collateral damage observed in this session\n\nThe defect is not confined to item listing. Reading this project's own quality gate under the default budget silently reshaped the measurement:\n\n    pm assurance run tracker-context-quality --trigger ci --dry-run --json --output-budget 600\n      -> verdict \"pass\", exit_code 0, assertions array length 2\n\n    pm assurance run tracker-context-quality --trigger ci --dry-run --json --output-budget unbounded\n      -> verdict \"pass\", exit_code 0, assertions array length 40\n\nThe scalar verdict was correct in both readings. The evidence set behind it was reduced by 95 percent with has_more carrying the only signal and no way to continue. A reviewer reading the budgeted form concludes the gate enforces two invariants when it enforces forty.\n\n## Why the fix belongs to the budget contract\n\nA cursor is a position in a total order. The budget truncation already knows the position at which it stopped compacting rows, because it names the compacted row paths. Emitting a cursor there is the same operation the limit path already performs. The contract question is what a continuation means when the budget rather than the caller chose the page size, and that is the declaration pm-5t33or owns, which is why this is ordered behind it."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: context,output-budget,pagination,scale
created_at: "2026-08-14T05:11:18.919Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-18T12:25:47.510Z"
