completed_at: "2026-08-18T12:25:46.204Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "A read truncated by the output budget emits a continuation cursor that resumes the same query at the first withheld row, on every row-producing surface that emits has_more; The envelope distinguishes limit truncation from budget truncation in the pagination contract itself, so a caller reading only the declared pagination keys can tell a resumable page from a terminal one; No recovery instruction for a budget truncation names an unbounded re-read as the sole path, and the declared recovery cost is bounded by a stated multiple of the budget rather than by the corpus; A regression test walks pm list-closed to completion on a workspace larger than the default budget using only cursors, and asserts total rows delivered equals total, with peak response size bounded; The assurance verdict surface is covered by the same contract, so a gate reading its own evidence rows under a budget either receives every assertion or receives a cursor to the rest"
parent: pm-9rxu
risk: high
confidence: 92
resolution: fixed
expected_result: Every budget-truncated read remains resumable within the same bounded cost and discloses why and how continuation works.
actual_result: "Universal command-bound output cursors now cover every declared row path, including assurance evidence, with stable replay, stale/mismatch refusals, compact cross-transport recovery, and bounded full-walk acceptance."
