comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-14T06:51:28.004Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: list-all and --no-truncate now imply unbounded cost unless an explicit canonical budget overrides them; budget-compacted producer pages rebase next_cursor to the last retained item and disclose structured CLI/SDK/MCP recovery, preventing skipped hidden rows. MCP outputBudget now accepts the same unbounded escape hatch as CLI and SDK."
  "2026-08-14T07:55:44.180Z","harness:codex","Tranche evidence: top-level item producer pages now rebase a continuation cursor to the last retained row and disclose structured CLI/SDK/MCP recovery; list-all and --no-truncate returned 45/45 rows in a packed temporary project; linked tests and exact coverage pass. Residual acceptance remains for cursor-native continuation across every nested row-producing and assurance-verdict surface, so this item returns open."
  "2026-08-14T09:31:37.946Z","harness:codex","Final verification evidence for the delivered tranche: the exact uncommitted head passed 493 test files / 7,288 tests with exact coverage 52,942/52,942 statements, 38,963/38,963 branches, 10,875/10,875 functions, and 51,131/51,131 lines. Lint, zero-clone jscpd over 991 files, 100% docstrings, SDK parity, surface replication, bounded-output/token, graph, record-integrity, and contract snapshot gates passed. The item remains open and unclaimed because recursive continuation across every row-producing and assurance surface is intentionally not claimed complete by this tranche."
  "2026-08-14T10:02:41.914Z","harness:codex","Delivery closeout 2026-08-14: PR #1013 exact implementation head cd6d04061 merged to main as a7f68fb84 after the full local and hosted matrices passed. Cursor rebasing, unbounded recovery parity, shared public cursor decoding, and MCP schema parity shipped; CodeRabbit confirmed the review fixes with no remaining actionable issue. This item remains open and unclaimed for the documented nested and assurance continuation residual."
  "2026-08-14T11:04:47.534Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-14: coupled SDK/CLI/MCP tranche will add resumable universal output continuation for budget-compacted declared row paths, with assurance assertions as the live proof and exact first-withheld-row replay. Reproduced tracker-context-quality at --output-budget 600: 2/40 assertions survived and no cursor was emitted."
  "2026-08-14T12:16:57.559Z","harness:codex","Architecture evidence: moved the continuation module into src/sdk/read-output/ so src/sdk remains at the enforced 120-file ceiling; tracker file provenance migrated through pm files. The real tracker-context gate had detected the stale old path and orphaned new path, proving the validation ratchets work."
  "2026-08-14T12:39:42.150Z","harness:codex","Token-efficiency evidence: the agent token-surface gate initially rejected repeated opaque cursors in the contracts summary. Recovery now carries one compact 96-bit-fingerprint cursor with explicit CLI/SDK/MCP bindings, removing protocol duplication; the unchanged 10,064-byte summary ceiling passes without raising the baseline."
  "2026-08-14T12:57:32.343Z","harness:codex","Final verification: universal budget cursors resume declared list, context, contracts, object-row, and assurance collections at the exact first withheld row; a real temporary CLI walked 12 closed items with no overlap and exact parity with the unbounded baseline while keeping every response below 12 KB. Full repository verification passed 494 files / 7,295 tests and exact 53,025 statements, 39,093 branches, 10,900 functions, and 51,207 lines."
  "2026-08-14T13:21:18.071Z","harness:codex","Review triage: accepted cursor-size prevalidation, missing post-budget nested-path cardinality, and weak object-map assertions. Refused next_cursor removal because continuation_kind plus recovery bindings explicitly define how the universal cursor is consumed; refused pre-merge terminal-state rollback because the repository workflow closes verified work before commit/PR and requires only active edits in progress."
  "2026-08-14T13:34:53.418Z","harness:codex","Review verification: decoder now refuses cursor inputs above the established 4,096-character bound before allocation/parsing; object-map replay asserts the exact first withheld key and zero overlap; nested non-row budget compaction asserts continuation_available=false. The separate missing-path report is not reachable for declared row paths because the resolver only traverses object owners and those owners are not compactible collections. Final exact coverage is 53,028/53,028 statements, 39,095/39,095 branches, 10,900/10,900 functions, and 51,210/51,210 lines; full lint/static, context evaluation, token surfaces, tracker assurance, and contracts pass."
  "2026-08-18T08:55:32.913Z","harness:codex","Fresh recurrence evidence 2026-08-18: pm validate --check-resolution --check-history-drift --json used a 9,000-token default budget, then reported has_more/truncated with continuation_kind=none and prescribed --output-budget 1200, a lower budget than the failed read. The compacted diagnostic rows were non-resumable despite output_budget_truncation naming them. Core health and history drift were clean; this is a recovery-envelope residual in the canonical closed lineage, so no duplicate item was created or reopened."
  "2026-08-18T12:13:57.414Z","harness:codex","Evidence: implemented validate diagnostic row contracts atop the universal read-output SDK and extended nested row traversal across numeric array segments. Real repository acceptance with --output-budget 1200 now returns continuation_kind=output_cursor for checks.0.details.missing_resolution_rows, retains 9 of 295 rows, reports 286 remaining, and a same-budget cursor retry begins at the next disjoint row. Focused governance continuation tests cover resolution/history rows, pre-existing/absent/already-declared contracts, and invalid array paths. Exact coverage passed 55061/55061 statements, 41094/41094 branches, 11376/11376 functions, 53146/53146 lines; the cold-read performance sentinel passed independently in 5.17s under its unchanged 10s ceiling."
  "2026-08-18T12:25:37.771Z","harness:codex","Hosted governance correction: exact-head run 32136048605 correctly blocked because the 2026-08-18 recurrence closure lacked post-epoch defect evidence. Classified it as production_defect and linked the validate-read-output-continuation negative control, focused local test, exact coverage, defect-evidence gate, and hosted static/coverage owners. This strengthens the gate record; it does not waive or bypass the failure."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-14T07:55:47.229Z","harness:codex",Budget compaction must rebase a producer cursor to the last row actually emitted. Returning the producer's original page-end cursor after dropping rows creates a silent data-loss gap even when has_more remains true.
